# Modal overlays

Build every dialog backdrop with `ModalOverlay` from
`@/app/components/ModalOverlay`. Do not hand-roll
`fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center`.

A fixed element does not scroll. When the panel grows taller than the window —
a modal that reveals fields as you fill it in, a short laptop window, a
zoomed-in browser — the overflow becomes unreachable and only the page behind
moves, so the submit button cannot be clicked at all. This shipped once in the
cancellation modal: choosing "Refund Requested" added an amount and a MID, and
users on laptops could not reach Confirm.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — buttons vanish once the panel outgrows the window
<div className="fixed inset-0 z-[200] flex items-center justify-center bg-black/50 p-4">
  <div className="w-full max-w-md rounded-lg bg-white p-6">{/* … */}</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD
<ModalOverlay labelledBy="my-title" onBackdropClick={() => setOpen(false)}>
  <div className="w-full max-w-md rounded-lg bg-white p-6">{/* … */}</div>
</ModalOverlay>
```

Notes:

- Omit `onBackdropClick` for a dialog that must be answered, not dismissed.
- `className` carries only stacking and tint, e.g. `"z-[245] bg-black/40"`.
- The panel needs no `onClick` stopPropagation; the backdrop check handles it.
- If the panel's height varies a lot, also cap it and pin its actions so the
  buttons never need scrolling:
  `flex max-h-[calc(100vh-2rem)] flex-col` with the body in an
  `overflow-y-auto` div and the buttons in a sibling below it. See the
  cancellation modal in `app/(crm)/clients/[id]/ClientStageHeader.tsx`.
- Older overlays elsewhere still use the raw pattern; convert them when you
  touch that file.

Verify at a short window (about 620px tall, and 420px for a stress test) that
the primary action is on screen, not just present in the DOM.
